ures are in dynamic equilibrium with each other.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f342ee0e063d924faa0"}, {"id": "b71fcd", "text": "Each structure exists for equal amount of time.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f342ee0e063d924faa1"}, {"id": "b44e4d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>CO</mi><mn>3</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math>&nbsp;has a single structure i.e., resonance hybrid of the above three structures.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f342ee0e063d924faa2"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f342ee0e063d924faa3", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfaf4"], "topics": ["60e567fc499d1e49588fa045"], "concepts": ["6117b608478ae845c43c637b"], "question": {"text": "If Dichloromethane (DCM) and water <math><msub><mrow><mtext>H</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mtext>O</mtext></math> are used for differential extraction, which one of the following statements is correct?"}, "options": [{"id": "8afcef", "text": "DCM and <math><msub><mrow><mtext>H</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mtext>O</mtext></math> would stay as upper and lower layer respectively in the separating funnel (S.F.)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f342ee0e063d924faa4"}, {"id": "ac8f03", "text": "DCM and  <math><msub><mrow><mtext>H</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mtext>O</mtext></math>  will be miscible clearly", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f342ee0e063d924faa5"}, {"id": "878801", "text": "DCM and <math><msub><mrow><mtext>H</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mtext>O</mtext></math> would stay as lower and upper layer respectively in the S.F", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f342ee0e063d924faa6"}, {"id": "c27ef3", "text": "DCM and  <math><msub><mrow><mtext>H</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mtext>O</mtext></math>  will make turbid/colloidal mixture", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f342ee0e063d924faa7"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "60